    "body": "I think the problem you are seeing is because that script is testing if the `true` command  passed not the `false` command, the `if` just checks the exit code of the command/function that was run, see below.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n#!/bin/bash\r\nset -euo pipefail\r\n\r\nfn() {\r\n  echo \"start\"\r\n  if /bin/true; then # a passing command\r\n    echo \"This should always get printed\"\r\n  fi\r\n  if /bin/false; then # a failing command\r\n    echo \"This should never get printed\"\r\n  fi\r\n  echo \"end\"\r\n}\r\n\r\nfn\r\n```",
    "created_at": "2020-06-11T07:30:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T07:30:15Z",
